 decision/agent-run-holds-no-process · Agent-run holds no process — The agent-run script starts, polls and listens on nothing (no daemon, PID file, status endpoint, port or socket) and reads no environment variable of its own; the stand checks it runs boot in process. · except: stand_session_lifecycle, stand_session_quiet and the session selection's cli_flow flows start and stop a session host process and its socket, a surface of the session library, not of this contract
+decision/box-presence-read-with-display · Box presence read with computed display — A check asking whether a node has a box reads the node's computed display beside its client rect. · why: A node a restyle turns display none keeps the client rect it last laid out at.
 decision/bridge-tests-without-widening · Bridge tests without widening visibility — The event-bridge tests sit in a cfg(test) child module of the Dioxus document module, and no function under test gains a constructor or a pub for them. · why: DioxusEventHandler's two fields are private to that module and it has no constructor · except: the one cfg(test) shim, DioxusDocument::dispatch_to_vdom, which dispatches a chain into the vdom for a bridge test
@@ -323,3 +324,3 @@
 decision/harness-graph-tests-enable-accessibility · Harness graph unit tests turn accessibility on — A harness unit test of the UI graph turns the accessibility feature on through its dev-dependency, for the test build only. · why: A per-package test build leaves the accessibility feature off, and the UI graph is gated by it.
-decision/mutation-controlled-tests · Tests controlled red-before-green — A new check is controlled: a named mutation of what it guards turns it red, and the restored tree reads green again; a control that removes a bound loosens it to twice the budget rather than removing it, so the mutated run stays bounded.
+decision/mutation-controlled-tests · Tests controlled red-before-green — A new check is controlled: a named mutation of what it guards turns it red, a case it leaves green widened until it does, and the restored tree reads green; a control removing a bound loosens it to twice the budget instead, so the mutated run stays bounded.
 decision/no-change-read-control-needs-pending-work · Control of a no-change read needs pending work — A control of a read that must change nothing gives the read pending work that a pass would apply, so a read that ran a pass would be seen. · why: A pump on a settled screen is invisible, so a control built on one reads nothing and is no control.
